It handles decoding by replacing all `+` characters with spaces, and then applying `decodeURIComponent` to both the key and value.

It manages data structure accumulation: if a key already exists in the resulting object, it checks if it's already an array. If not, it converts the existing value to an array and pushes the new value; if it is already an array, it pushes the new value. Finally, it cleans up any single-item arrays to return a plain string, fulfilling all specified requirements.

